---
title: About
---
This catalogue is intended for researchers. It aims to be exhaustive and follows the model of critical thematic catalogues (Nectoux for Fauré, Kayas for Ligeti).

The two red strokes that open each entry echo the mark Greif drew in red pencil in the top left corner of some of his manuscripts.

## Abbreviations and conventions

| Abbreviation | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| Th | Thematic catalogue number. Letters (a, b) mark versions or derived works. Numbering is not yet final: each entry has a permanent identifier, used in the page address, and “Th” cross-references are recomputed automatically. |
| CaG | Olivier Greif's autograph catalogue. |
| F-Pbmgf | Paris, Bibliothèque musicale La Grange-Fleuret, Olivier Greif collection. |
| F-Pmm | [to be specified] |
| Ms. | Manuscript. |
| f. | Folio. |
| rº / vº | Recto / verso. |
| mes. | Bars (mesures). |
| mvt | Movement. |
| s. d. | Undated. |
| « … » | Diplomatic transcription (title page, autograph inscriptions). |
| \| | Line break in the transcription. |
| [ … ] | Editorial restoration or comment. |
| [sic] | Spelling of the original. |

## Incipits

Musical incipits are engraved in Finale and exported as PNG. Each image is uploaded through Keystatic, from the work's entry: movement, « Incipit musical » field.
